<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Georgia Salzburgers</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a> Salzburgers were Lutheran refugees from the Archbishopric of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salzburg">Salzburg</a>, expelled by Archbishop <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leopold-anton-von-firmian">Leopold Anton von Firmian</a> in 1731–1732, who settled in the Province of Georgia from 1734. They founded Ebenezer near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/savannah">Savannah</a>, where they farmed, raised <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk">silk</a> and for years opposed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a>. Their <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> Lutheran Church, completed in 1769, still stands.</p></div>
